DESCRIPTION:This workshop considers the genre differences between the dissertation and a final\, publishable scholarly monograph. We consider how to rework your finished dissertation with an eye towards transforming your research into a more refined and confident argument. This workshop also explores the book proposal as is the essential first step towards publishing in the humanities. We aim to demystify what university press editors are actually looking for in a book proposal\, including audience\, market fit\, and chapter structure\, and help participants understand what to expect from the university press book publishing process. \n\n \n\nFor in-person attendance:\n\nPlease have your FSU Card ready for check-in.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Peer Review\, Editorial Decisions & Responding to Reviewers  
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/F-26-UAP-Reviewers-Oct20
CATEGORIES:Professional Development
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Seminars
END:VEVENT
