DESCRIPTION:Join FSU Libraries and the School of Information for "From UFOs to UAPs: Science\, Sensationalism\, and Things That Go Blip in the Night." This interdisciplinary panel conversation brings together faculty members from across Florida State University to analyze the UAP phenomenon through multiple academic lenses. Panelists will discuss the validity of recorded sightings\, the long and fraught history of the field\, and break down how journalistic framing and digital platforms influence public perception. \n\nWhether you are a curious skeptic or a seasoned researcher\, join us for an engaging discussion on what lies behind the headlines\, the hype\, and the things that go blip in the night. Light lunch will be provided for attendees at 11:30am\, with the official panel starting at 12pm. \n\nNote: Registration for this event is required because lunch is provided. \n\nYou can also check out more information about the event and related UAP resources on our online guide! \n\n \n\nPanelists: \n\nGretchen Stahman (FSU School of Information) \n\nRonald Doel (FSU Department of History) \n\nJeremiah Murphy (FSU Department of Physics) \n\nAnnie Zhang (FSU School of Communication) \n\nTim Spuck (Associated Universities\, Inc.)
GEO:30.44302;-84.295059
LOCATION:Robert Manning Strozier Library\, Basement Level\, Bradley Reading Room
SUMMARY:From UFOs to UAPs: Science\, Sensationalism\, and Things That Go Blip in the Night
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/UAPpanel-Fall2026
CATEGORIES:Academic/Registrar
CATEGORIES:Panel
